#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# factor_square_free_list

#% text
# `factor_square_free_list(p)` gives `[[c, 1], [f1, k1], ...]` with `p = c f1^k1 ...`, the `fi` square free and relatively prime, in order of increasing multiplicity.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
factor_square_free_list(x^2*(x + 1)^3*(x - 2))
#% output
#= [[1, 1], [-2 + x, 1], [x, 2], [1 + x, 3]]

#% cell
factor_square_free_list(x^3 - x^2 - 5*x - 3)
#% output
#= [[1, 1], [-3 + x, 1], [1 + x, 2]]

#% cell
factor_square_free_list(6*x^2)
#% output
#= [[6, 1], [x, 2]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `factor_square_free`, `factor`
